tip: | Look at the motorcycle. | The same two wheels as the bicycle, with something heavy between them. Where the bicycle was air, this is solid.
tip: 1 | Mass between the wheels. | The block-in fills the frame. Tank, seat and engine are one lump that leans slightly forward.
tip: 3 | The tank catches the light. | It is the only smooth rounded part, so it gets the widest ramp and a highlight along the top.
tip: 4 | Dark details on dark. | The engine is two steps of gray with a row of fins. Near black needs only a little contrast to read.
